{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Make Buses Safer for Babies and More Accessible for Parents and Pushchairs",
        "additional_details": "Parents travelling with babies and toddlers often face the difficult choice of removing their child from a secured pushchair or being unable to board due to a lack of space. Babies deserve safe travel too. We want buses designed with more dedicated pushchair space and properly approved child-restraint seating, while protecting wheelchair users\u2019 priority access. Public transport should work safely for families as well as disabled passengers.",
        "background": "Require bus operators and manufacturers to provide safer, more accessible travel for parents with babies and toddlers, including additional pushchair space and the introduction of approved child safety seats on buses, without compromising wheelchair accessibility.",
